        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "historical-geography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Historical Geography and the Feudal World - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Problem 3: Allodial Land\nLand held outright with no overlord. The exception that proves the rule.\n```\n  FEUDAL LAND:           ALLODIAL LAND:\n  Lord → Vassal          Owner holds free\n  (service owed)         (no service owed)\n  Most land in           Rarer — old Frankish\n  feudal Europe          freeholders, some\n                         Swiss communes,\n                         Norwegian odal rights\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#032",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:historical-geography:00-overview, git-history:historical-geography:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "historical-geography/00-OVERVIEW.md",
